On 18 January 2020, the [[Pact of Unity|Unity Pact]] of MAS bases elected [[David Choquehuanca]] and Andrónico Rodríguez as presidential and vice-presidential candidates. On 19 January, Evo Morales announced that [[Luis Alberto Arce Catacora]] and David Choquehuanca would be the party's presidential and vice presidential candidates. This was following a vote by those members of MAS leadership present in Buenos Aires the previous day.{{sfn|Infobae|2020}} This difference caused some friction among different sections of the MAS bases, including the Barolina Sisa and Tupac Katari Federation who rejected these selections.<ref>{{cite web| url=https://www.paginasiete.bo/nacional/2020/1/20/bartolinas-campesinos-afines-al-mas-rechazan-el-binomio-de-evo-244043.html| title=The social and peasant organizations of the department of La Paz feel betrayed by the decision of Evo Morales| language=es| date=21 January 2020| access-date=23 January 2020| archive-date=21 October 2020| archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201021153145/https://www.paginasiete.bo/nacional/2020/1/20/bartolinas-campesinos-afines-al-mas-rechazan-el-binomio-de-evo-244043.html| url-status=dead}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.paginasiete.bo/nacional/2020/1/22/morales-defiende-arce-pero-surgen-mas-voces-de-rechazo-244242.html|title=Morales defends Arce, but more voices of rejection arise|date=22 January 2020|language=es}}</ref> On 21 January, the Central Obrera Boliviana (COB) supplied a third candidacy combination of Choquehuanca paired with Orlando Gutiérrez. MAS President of the Senate, Eva Copa, said the matter was not yet closed and would be decided by a further meeting of the Unity Pact.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.la-razon.com/nacional/Copa-Pacto-Unidad-posicion-binomio-elecciones-bolivia_0_3298470201.html | title=Copa MAS Binomial: We take it as a proposal to be debated | date=22 January 2020 | language=es | access-date=23 January 2020 | archive-date=23 January 2020 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200123180509/http://www.la-razon.com/nacional/Copa-Pacto-Unidad-posicion-binomio-elecciones-bolivia_0_3298470201.html | url-status=dead }}</ref> On 23 January, the Unity Pact ratified the Arce-Choquehuanca ticket chosen in Buenos Aires.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.paginasiete.bo/nacional/2020/1/23/pacto-de-unidad-acepta-el-binomio-arce-choquehuanca-244342.html|title=Unity pact accepts the Arce-Choquehuanca|language=es|date=23 January 2020}}</ref> On 24 January, a new right-wing political alliance called "We Believe" ("Creemos") was formed, and endorsed the [[Luis Fernando Camacho|Camacho]]-[[:w:es:Marco Pumari|Pumari]] ticket.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://eldeber.com.bo/163754_tres-partidos-se-unen-para-postular-al-binomio-camacho-pumari#.XisiUYnCbHo.facebook|title=Three parties join to endorse the Camacho-Pumari ticket|language=es|date=24 January 2020}}</ref> By the registration deadline, the Supreme Electoral Tribunal (TSE) announced that five political coalitions had been registered.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/TSEBolivia/status/1220937944363687936|trans-title=These are all alliances that submitted their applications for registration before the Supreme Electoral Tribunal.|publisher=TSE Bolivia|website=Twitter|title=Estas son todas las alianzas que presentaron sus solicitudes de registro ante el Tribunal Supremo Electoral.|language=es|date=25 January 2020}}</ref> However, on 31 January the TSE announced that the coalition "United People" had been disqualified after not submitting the required documents.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/TSEBolivia/status/1223408206023667712/photo/1|title=Estas son las Alianzas Políticas habilitadas para las Elecciones Generales 2020.|language=es|date=25 January 2020}}</ref>

In July 2020, a lawsuit was filed by four separate political parties (among others) with the Supreme Electoral Court asking it to disqualify Arce from standing in the presidential election. The lawsuit stated Arce had released an opinion poll on the presidential race outside the time frame allowed. In 2015, a similar complaint was filed against Ernesto Suárez, leader of the opposition UD bench in the Department of Beni, regarding release of polls by outgoing governor campaign manager Carmelo Lens. This resulted in Suárez and 227 other UD candidates having their legal status cancelled and removed from the election.<ref>{{cite web| url=https://www.paginasiete.bo/nacional/2020/7/27/caso-arce-es-bumeran-para-el-mas-pero-afirman-que-se-le-debe-ganar-en-las-urnas-262535.html| title=Arce case is boomerang for MAS, but it must be won at the polls| language=es| date=27 July 2020| access-date=28 July 2020| archive-date=23 October 2020| archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201023053305/https://www.paginasiete.bo/nacional/2020/7/27/caso-arce-es-bumeran-para-el-mas-pero-afirman-que-se-le-debe-ganar-en-las-urnas-262535.html| url-status=dead}}</ref>

On 11 October, Jorge Quiroga announced that he and the political alliance he was heading were withdrawing from the race.<ref name=quirogaout>{{cite news |title="Tuto" declina su candidatura a siete días de los comicios |url=https://www.paginasiete.bo/nacional/2020/10/11/tuto-declina-su-candidatura-siete-dias-de-los-comicios-271162.html |access-date=11 October 2020 |work=www.paginasiete.bo |date=11 October 2020 |language=es |archive-date=21 October 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201021132126/https://www.paginasiete.bo/nacional/2020/10/11/tuto-declina-su-candidatura-siete-dias-de-los-comicios-271162.html |url-status=dead }}</ref>

