==Debates==
During the 14 years and preceding period where Evo Morales was president and presidential candidate, Morales declined to take part in any public debate with any of the other candidates, making the justification that he only "debates with the people".<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.paginasiete.bo/especial02/2020/10/4/el-esperado-debate-llega-en-el-trayecto-decisivo-del-voto-270272.html|title=The long-awaited debate comes on the decisive path of the vote|language=es|date=4 October 2020|website=www.paginasiete.bo|access-date=8 October 2020|archive-date=26 October 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201026184143/https://www.paginasiete.bo/especial02/2020/10/4/el-esperado-debate-llega-en-el-trayecto-decisivo-del-voto-270272.html|url-status=dead}}</ref> In January 2020, interim president Jeanine Áñez submitted legislation to make this a compulsory requirement for presidential candidates in upcoming elections, but this was rejected by the MAS-controlled Senate.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.lostiempos.com/actualidad/pais/20191231/anez-envia-alp-proyecto-ley-que-plantea-debate-obligatorio-candidatos |website=www.lostiempos.com |language=es |title=Áñez submits a bill to assembly that raises mandatory debate between candidates|date=31 December 2019 }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.lostiempos.com/actualidad/pais/20200117/anez-apela-alp-aprobar-ley-debate-obligatorio-rumbo-elecciones |title=Áñez appeals to ALP to approve bill on obligatory electoral debates|date=13 January 2020 |language=es |website=www.lostiempos.com}}</ref>

A historic debate which would gather all the presidential candidates together on the same stage for the first time in almost two decades was announced on 6 September, organised by the association of Bolivian Journalists, media organisations and others. The debate was covered by more than 80 national and international media and an audience of more than five million people was expected. The event also had the backing of 50 national institutions and the financial and technical support of the European Union, International Idea, the Konrad Adenauer Foundation and the embassies of Canada, Germany and Switzerland. When it aired, it achieved record viewing numbers.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://eldeber.com.bo/pais/anuncian-gran-debate-presidencial-para-el-4-de-octubre_199225|date=6 September 2020|website=El Deber|language=es|title=Great Presidential Debate announced for 4th October}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |title=Debate presidencial alcanza audiencia de más de 2 millones personas en Facebook |url=https://www.paginasiete.bo/nacional/2020/10/6/debate-presidencial-alcanza-audiencia-de-mas-de-millones-personas-en-facebook-270545.html |access-date=8 October 2020 |work=[[Página Siete]] |date=6 October 2020 |language=es}}</ref> From the beginning, however, the MAS candidate Luis Arce was reluctant to make a commitment to attend, with he and MAS first placing conditions on attending, such as they not be subject to insults, and later claiming a clash with a planned interview with the television network Red Uno (which the network later moved to allow free up the MAS candidate).<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.paginasiete.bo/nacional/2020/9/23/en-11-dias-arce-mas-pusieron-cuatro-condiciones-para-debatir-269038.html|title=In 11 days, Arce-MAS put 4 conditions for debate|date=23 September 2020|language=es|website=www.paginasiete.bo.com}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.paginasiete.bo/nacional/2020/10/3/arce-patea-tablero-del-debate-pone-excusa-para-no-asistir-270229.html|title=Arce overturns debate podium and gives excuse for not attending|language=es|date=2 October 2020}}</ref> On the night of the broadcast, both he and Creemos candidate, Luis Camacho, did not attend. Camacho said he did not attend because he had been deceived that Mesa would also not be attending.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://correodelsur.com/politica/20201005_creemos-afirma-que-camacho-no-asistio-al-debate-porque-fue-enganado.html|website=Correa del Sur|language=es|title=Creemos confirm that Camacho did not attend because he was "deceived".}}</ref> A panel of 40 analysts surveyed by Pagina Siete indicated that Mesa came out as the most favourable candidate from this debate.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.paginasiete.bo/nacional/2020/10/5/de-40-analistas-69-elige-mesa-como-ganador-del-debate-270391.html|language=es|date=5 October 2020|title=Of 40 analysts, 69% choose Mesa as the winner of the debate.|access-date=8 October 2020|archive-date=22 October 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201022061247/https://www.paginasiete.bo/nacional/2020/10/5/de-40-analistas-69-elige-mesa-como-ganador-del-debate-270391.html|url-status=dead}}</ref>

While Arce did not attend the debate on 4 October, he did attend another broadcast the previous day in which all presidential candidates were present. This was organised by the Federation of Municipal Associations (FAM) and the Confederation of Universities of Bolivia (CUB).<ref>{{cite news |last1=Ramos |first1=Daniel |title='We're not used to debating': Rare Bolivia election standoff fizzles as vote nears |url=https://www.reuters.com/article/us-bolivia-election-debate-idUSKBN26P0M6 |access-date=8 October 2020 |work=Reuters |date=4 October 2020 |language=en}}</ref> The debate format received criticism for not allowing candidates to respond to each other as well as accusations that the organisers were pro-MAS.<ref>{{cite news |title=Debate presidencial» de FAM-CUB genera críticas al formato de cuestionarios sin discusión |url=http://bolivianueva.press/debate-presidencial-de-fam-cub-genera-criticas-al-formato-de-cuestionarios-sin-discusion/ |access-date=8 October 2020 |work=Bolivia Nueva Tus historias... tus noticias... |publisher=Bolivia Nueva |date=4 October 2020 |language=es |archive-date=21 October 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201021182624/http://bolivianueva.press/debate-presidencial-de-fam-cub-genera-criticas-al-formato-de-cuestionarios-sin-discusion/ |url-status=dead }}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.la-razon.com/opinion/2020/10/07/el-debate-que-no-fue/|title=The Debate that was not|language=es|website=La Razon|date=5 October 2020}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://eldeber.com.bo/pais/politicos-acusan-al-mas-de-amanar-debate-del-sabado_203226|website=El Deber|title=Politicians accuse MAS of rigging Saturday's debate|date=4 October 2020|language=es}}</ref> Criticisms included that it was not a debate, but a "monologue", "fashion show" and "propaganda" and that the definition of debate should include at least some form of interaction, interrogation, discussion or confrontation between candidates. The format of the debate was in some part determined by conditions set by Luis Arce to guarantee his attendance that "no personal or partisan allusions were allowed", i.e. no direct criticisms of other candidates or of their party.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.erbol.com.bo/el-%C3%A1nfora-1/%E2%80%9Cdebate-presidencial-de-fam-cub-genera-cr%C3%ADticas-al-formato-de-cuestionarios-sin|title="Presidential Debate" of FAM-CUB generates criticism of the questionnaire format without discussion|language=es|date=3 Oct 2020|website=ERBOL}}</ref>

