==Conduct==

Election day was relatively peaceful. Deputy security minister Wilson Santamaria said that two people tried to interfere with ballot papers in capital La Paz, but they were apprehended.<ref>{{cite web|date=2020-10-19|title=Polls start closing in 'calm' Bolivian general election|url=https://www.deccanherald.com/international/polls-start-closing-in-calm-bolivian-general-election-903950.html|access-date=2020-10-19|website=Deccan Herald|language=en}}</ref>

The head of Supreme Electoral Tribunal (TSE) commended the conduct of the polls, saying that "election day was a successful day for democracy."<ref>{{Cite web|last=Pacheco|first=Valeria|date=19 October 2020|title=Bolivia 'has recovered democracy', says Arce as exit poll suggests win|url=https://news.yahoo.com/bolivians-vote-election-expected-bring-122733945.html|access-date=2020-10-26|publisher=[[Agence France-Presse]]|language=en-US|via=Yahoo! News}}</ref> The United Nations applauded the elections as having occurred in "an orderly manner, in a climate of tranquility and respect for human rights".<ref>{{cite web|date=2020-10-19|title=Naciones Unidas aplaude orden y tranquilidad en los comicios generales de Bolivia|url=https://www.paginasiete.bo/nacional/2020/10/19/naciones-unidas-aplaude-orden-tranquilidad-en-los-comicios-generales-de-bolivia-272043.html|access-date=2020-10-19|website=Pagina Siete|language=es}}</ref> The [[European Union]] congratulated Bolivia for the safe conduct of its elections as it awaited the results of the TSE.<ref>{{cite web|last=Cortez Becerra|first=Esmir|date=19 October 2020|title=La Unión Europea felicita a Bolivia y pide esperar los resultados oficiales de las elecciones|url=https://eldeber.com.bo/usted-elige/la-union-europea-felicita-a-bolivia-y-pide-esperar-los-resultados-oficiales-de-las-elecciones_205226|website=El Deber|language=es}}</ref>

During the vote count, the TSE received complaints of fraud from the separatist movement in Santa Cruz.{{citation needed|date=October 2020}} 

On 22 October, Bolivian mining union leader and previously proposed MAS vice-presidential candidate Orlando Gutiérrez suffered a head wound and was admitted to hospital. Although he was reported to be "stable, conscious and out of risk" shortly afterwards, on 28 October he was reported to have died in hospital. Information circulating on social media claimed an attack from a group calling themselves "pititas" in which he was beaten. Other sources say that it was the result of a brawl between different factions of MAS during a victory celebration. No criminal complaint was made and the body buried without an autopsy. An investigation was opened following his death, although previous attempts to investigate were denied and the diagnosis was kept confidential with no visitors allowed.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.paginasiete.bo/seguridad/2020/10/30/entierran-gutierrez-en-oruro-sin-autopsia-legal-entre-dudas-273310.html|title=Gutiérrez is buried in Oruro without legal autopsy and between doubts|language=es|date=30 October 2020|website=www.paginasiete.bo|access-date=30 October 2020|archive-date=1 November 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201101081651/https://www.paginasiete.bo/seguridad/2020/10/30/entierran-gutierrez-en-oruro-sin-autopsia-legal-entre-dudas-273310.html|url-status=dead}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://eldeber.com.bo/pais/familiares-se-opusieron-al-levantamiento-y-a-la-autopsia-del-cadaver-del-minero-orlando-gutierrez_206645|title=Family members opposed the collection and autopsy of the corpse of miner Orlando Gutiérrez|date=29 October 2020|language=es|website=www.eldeber.com.bo}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.atb.com.bo/sociedad/muere-el-l%C3%ADder-minero-orlando-guti%C3%A9rrez|date=28 October 2020|language=es|website=www.atb.com|title=Mining leader Orlando Gutiérrez dies|access-date=30 October 2020|archive-date=1 November 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201101021747/https://www.atb.com.bo/sociedad/muere-el-l%C3%ADder-minero-orlando-guti%C3%A9rrez|url-status=dead}}</ref>

== International observers ==
Representatives of the [[United States Agency for International Development]] (USAID) and the [[Organization of American States]] (OAS) arrived in Bolivia on 9 January 2020 to discuss monitoring the elections that were initially planned for 3 May.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.paginasiete.bo/nacional/2020/1/9/eeuu-envia-tecnicos-para-evaluar-apoyo-en-comicios-242915.html|title=US sends technicians to evaluate support in elections|date=9 January 2020|language=es}}</ref> USAID had been expelled in 2013 by the MAS government.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://eldeber.com.bo/edicion-impresa/el-mas-declaro-la-guerra-a-las-agencias-de-eeuu_161650|title=MAS declared war on US agencies|date=5 January 2020|language=es}}</ref>

International teams from the [[Carter Center]], Inter-American Union of Electoral Organizations (UNIORE) and Association of Electoral Organizations of South America were also approved as electoral observers by the TSE. Local initiatives from within Bolivia including La Ruta de la Democracia and Observe Bolivia have also been approved and will be observing the elections.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Vargas |first1=Luis Marcelo Tedesqui |title=Para el TSE, la candidata María de la Cruz Bayá sigue en carrera |url=https://eldeber.com.bo/pais/para-el-tse-la-candidata-maria-de-la-cruz-baya-sigue-en-carrera_204023 |publisher=[[El Deber]] |access-date=10 October 2020 |language=es |date=10 October 2020}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |title=Cinco misiones internacionales de observación vigilarán comicios |url=https://www.paginasiete.bo/nacional/2020/9/30/los-comicios-en-bolivia-contaran-con-cinco-misiones-internacionales-de-observacion-269892.html |access-date=10 October 2020 |work=Pagina Siete |date=30 September 2020 |language=es |archive-date=11 October 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201011121558/https://www.paginasiete.bo/nacional/2020/9/30/los-comicios-en-bolivia-contaran-con-cinco-misiones-internacionales-de-observacion-269892.html |url-status=dead }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title="Observa Bolivia" will contribute to the transparency of the electoral process and democracy in Bolivia {{!}} International IDEA |url=https://www.idea.int/news-media/news/%E2%80%9Cobserva-bolivia%E2%80%9D-will-contribute-transparency-electoral-process-and-democracy |website=www.idea.int |access-date=10 October 2020 |date=10 September 2020}}</ref> The OAS mission of observers consisted of 40 experts of 12 different nationalities.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.paginasiete.bo/especial02/2020/10/14/oea-ya-observa-los-comicios-convoca-preservar-la-paz-271451.html|title=OAS already observes the elections and calls to preserve the peace|date=14 October 2020|language=es|access-date=19 October 2020|archive-date=19 October 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201019190509/https://www.paginasiete.bo/especial02/2020/10/14/oea-ya-observa-los-comicios-convoca-preservar-la-paz-271451.html|url-status=dead}}</ref> The [[European Union]] (EU) announced on 8 September that it would be sending a team of five or six experts to observe the 18 October elections.<ref>{{cite web |title=La Unión Europea enviará una misión de expertos a las elecciones de Bolivia del 18 de octubre |url=https://www.infobae.com/america/america-latina/2020/09/08/la-union-europea-enviara-una-mision-de-expertos-a-las-elecciones-de-bolivia-del-18-de-octubre/ |website=infobae |access-date=10 September 2020 |language=es-ES |date=8 September 2020}}</ref> The Carter Centre sent two experts in electoral analysis.<ref name="observadores">{{cite web|date=13 October 2020|title=TSE, ONU y UE respaldan elecciones limpias, ante denuncias del MAS|url=https://www.lostiempos.com/actualidad/pais/20201013/tse-onu-ue-respaldan-elecciones-limpias-denuncias-del-mas|website=Los Tiempos|language=es}}</ref>

On 14 October 2020, the [[Progressive International]] sent an observer group made up of three national legislators from Greece, Poland and Spain, stating that they are "particularly concerned about the integrity of the presidential elections in Bolivia".<ref>{{Cite web|date=14 October 2020|title=Progressive International election observer mission lands in Bolivia|url=https://progressive.international/movement/article/2020-10-14-progressive-international-election-observer-mission-lands-in-bolivia/en|access-date=2020-10-17|website=Progressive International|language=en}}</ref>

A delegation of observers from [[Argentina]] invited by the [[Plurinational Legislative Assembly]] was subject to controversy when one of the delegates, lawmaker [[Federico Fagioli]], was detained at La Paz Airport.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.telam.com.ar/notas/202010/525726-diputado-argentino-retenido-ilegalmente-bolivia.html|archivedate=2023-09-28|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20230928210630/https://www.telam.com.ar/notas/202010/525726-diputado-argentino-retenido-ilegalmente-bolivia.html|work=[[Télam]]|title=El Gobierno denunció que un diputado argentino fue retenido ilegalmente en Bolivia|date=17 October 2020|access-date=19 October 2020|language=es}}</ref> The Bolivian Minister of the Interior, Arturo Morillo, stated that Fagioli had been warned not to return to Bolivia after the lawmaker's participation in a previous Argentine delegation that visited the country following the ousting of Evo Morales in 2019, and that Fagioli was a "[[persona non grata]]" in Bolivia.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://elpais.com/internacional/2020-10-17/el-gobierno-de-bolivia-retiene-en-el-aeropuerto-de-la-paz-a-un-diputado-argentino.html|work=[[El País]]|title=El Gobierno de Bolivia retiene en el aeropuerto de La Paz a un diputado argentino|date=17 October 2020|access-date=19 October 2020|language=es|last=Molina|first=Fernando}}</ref> In addition to Fagioli's detention, other members of the Argentine delegation, including other lawmakers, were also allegedly mistreated by Bolivian security forces. The incident was harshly criticized by Argentine president [[Alberto Fernández]] and MAS candidate Luis Arce.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://cnnespanol.cnn.com/2020/10/17/presidente-de-argentina-denuncia-maltratos-a-delegacion-de-observadores-de-elecciones-en-bolivia/|work=[[CNN en Español]]|title=Presidente de Argentina denuncia maltratos a delegación de observadores de elecciones en Bolivia|date=17 October 2020|access-date=19 October 2020|language=es}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.telam.com.ar/notas/202010/525738-luis-arce-bolivia-mas-federico-fagioli.html|archivedate=2023-09-29|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20230929202941/https://www.telam.com.ar/notas/202010/525738-luis-arce-bolivia-mas-federico-fagioli.html|work=[[Télam]]|title=El candidato del MAS condenó el "maltrato" al diputado argentino retenido|date=17 October 2020|access-date=19 October 2020|language=es}}</ref>

A total of 110 international observers were accredited by the TSE to attend and analyse the results of the election.<ref name=observadores />

The OAS, the UN and UNIORE have all made public statements testifying to the validity of the elections and the lack of evidence of any irregularities.<ref>{{cite web|date=21 October 2020|title=La misión de observación de la OEA descarta 'acciones fraudulentas' en las elecciones|url=https://www.la-razon.com/nacional/2020/10/21/la-mision-de-observacion-de-la-oea-descarta-acciones-fraudulentas-en-las-elecciones/|access-date=21 October 2020|website=La Razón|language=es}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|date=19 October 2020|title=Uniore señala que no hay registro de irregularidades que deslegitimen la votación|url=https://www.paginasiete.bo/nacional/2020/10/19/uniore-senala-que-no-hay-registro-de-irregularidades-que-deslegitimen-la-votacion-272071.html|access-date=22 October 2020|website=Pagina Siete|language=es|archive-date=24 October 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201024191059/https://www.paginasiete.bo/nacional/2020/10/19/uniore-senala-que-no-hay-registro-de-irregularidades-que-deslegitimen-la-votacion-272071.html|url-status=dead}}</ref><ref name="nofraude">{{cite web|last=Tancara Castillo|first=Cándido|date=23 October 2020|title=ONU, OEA y Uniore descartan fraude en elecciones generales|url=https://www.paginasiete.bo/nacional/2020/10/23/onu-oea-uniore-descartan-fraude-en-elecciones-generales-272528.html|website=Pagina Siete|language=es|access-date=23 October 2020|archive-date=14 April 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210414225506/https://www.paginasiete.bo/nacional/2020/10/23/onu-oea-uniore-descartan-fraude-en-elecciones-generales-272528.html|url-status=dead}}</ref> The Carter Centre supported the results and transparency of the elections, with minor recommendations on further improvements. They also analysed online disinformation targeting the electoral process in the 3 months prior to the election and noted "a proliferation of disinformation aimed at eroding the reputations of candidates and the TSE".<ref>{{cite web|date=23 October 2020|title=Carter Center Commends Bolivians and the Electoral Tribunal on a Calm and Respectful Election|url=https://www.cartercenter.org/news/pr/2020/bolivia-102320.html|access-date=24 October 2020|website=The Carter Center}}</ref>

== Results ==
MAS, which improved its result over the annulled 2019 elections but still slightly reduced compared to [[2014 Bolivian general election|2014]], attained a majority on its own in both chambers, meaning there is no obstacle to passing laws, but the loss of the two-thirds enjoyed by the party since 2009 means that some functions of the legislature will require cross-party support. These include the appointment of certain authorities (such as the Ombudsman for Human Rights, Comptroller General and Attorney General), making reforms in the constitution, the approval of judges for the Judicial Branch of government and the censuring of a government minister. This is the first time since 2009 that these decisions cannot be made by the ruling party alone.<ref name=twothirds />

