=== Responses ===
Although the official results had not been expected for some days, quick counts performed by Ciesmori and ''Mi Voto Cuenta'' (My Vote Counts) agreed that Arce won the election in the first round.<ref name="Qcount"/><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.com/news/world-latin-america-54591963|title=Bolivia election: Exit polls suggest win for Luis Arce|date=19 October 2020|website=BBC}}</ref> The vote count could be attended by any member of the public and the tally sheets photographed for reasons of transparency.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.paginasiete.bo/nacional/2020/10/18/romero-destaca-asistencia-masiva-tranquilidad-en-la-jornada-electoral-271974.html|title=Romero highlights massive attendance and tranquility on election day|date=18 October 2020|language=es|access-date=19 October 2020|archive-date=19 October 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201019174234/https://www.paginasiete.bo/nacional/2020/10/18/romero-destaca-asistencia-masiva-tranquilidad-en-la-jornada-electoral-271974.html|url-status=dead}}</ref> President Áñez and former president [[Tuto Quiroga]], also both former presidential candidates in this election and opponents of MAS, congratulated Luis Arce as president elect while Evo Morales celebrated in Argentina<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.elalteno.com.bo/ciudad/20201019/evo-proclama-la-victoria-del-mas|title=Evo proclaims victory for MAS|date=19 October 2020|language=es|access-date=19 October 2020|archive-date=21 October 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201021162509/http://www.elalteno.com.bo/ciudad/20201019/evo-proclama-la-victoria-del-mas|url-status=dead}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.elalteno.com.bo/ciudad/20201019/presidenta-anez-felicita-arce-y-choquehuanca|title=Áñez congratulates Arce and Choquehuanca|date=19 October 2020|language=es|access-date=19 October 2020|archive-date=23 October 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201023101203/http://www.elalteno.com.bo/ciudad/20201019/presidenta-anez-felicita-arce-y-choquehuanca|url-status=dead}}</ref><ref name="Quiroga"/> [[Luis Almagro]], the Secretary-General of the OAS, also congratulated Luis Arce and David Choquehuanca on their victory, noting that democracy "will create a bright future for Bolivia."<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.paginasiete.bo/nacional/2020/10/19/almagro-felicita-al-binomio-del-mas-dice-que-el-pueblo-se-expreso-en-las-urnas-272058.html|title=Almagro congratulates the MAS team and says that "the people expressed themselves at the polls"|date=18 October 2020|language=es}}</ref> CC candidate Carlos Mesa recognised Arce as winner in the first round based on the preliminary results and accepted a mandate as the leader of the opposition.<ref name="MesaConc"/> On 23 October, after the completion of the official vote count, Creemos candidate Luis Camacho also publicly acknowledged the results.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.lostiempos.com/actualidad/pais/20201023/camacho-reconoce-resultados-nuestros-parlamentarios-electos-no-negociaran|title=Camacho acknowledges the results: "Our elected parliamentarians will not negotiate their vote"|date=23 October 2020|language=es}}</ref>

Political allies of Evo Morales, including [[Daniel Ortega]] and [[Rosario Murillo]] (President and Vice-President of Nicaragua), [[Andrés Manuel López Obrador]] (President of Mexico), [[Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva]] (former President of Brazil), [[Rafael Correa]] (former President of Ecuador), [[Nicolás Maduro]] ([[President of Venezuela]]), and [[Alberto Fernández]] and [[Cristina Kirchner]] (President and Vice-President of Argentina), congratulated the Arce-Choquehuanca ticket on their victory.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.paginasiete.bo/nacional/2020/10/19/correa-fernandez-lula-kirchner-maduro-felicitan-al-binomio-del-mas-272060.html|title=Correa, Fernández, Lula, Kirchner and Maduro congratulate the MAS joint ticket|date=18 October 2020|language=es|access-date=19 October 2020|archive-date=21 October 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201021153621/https://www.paginasiete.bo/nacional/2020/10/19/correa-fernandez-lula-kirchner-maduro-felicitan-al-binomio-del-mas-272060.html|url-status=dead}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.infobae.com/america/agencias/2020/10/19/nicaragua-felicita-a-morales-y-a-arce-por-incuestionable-triunfo-en-bolivia/|title=Nicaragua congratulates Morales and Arce for "unquestionable" triumph in Bolivia|date=19 October 2020|language=es}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.forbes.com.mx/noticias-lopez-obrador-felicita-a-luis-alberto-arce-por-triunfo-electoral-en-bolivia/|title=AMLO congratulates Arce, from the party of Evo Morales, for winning the presidency of Bolivia|date=19 October 2020|language=es}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.lavozdelsandinismo.com/nicaragua/2020-10-19/compartimos-la-alegria-del-pueblo-boliviano-que-hoy-ha-visto-triunfar-sus-suenos/|title=Gobierno de Nicaragua felicita con alegría al Presidente Electo Luis Arce de Bolivia|date=19 October 2020|language=es|access-date=20 October 2020|archive-date=21 October 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201021232951/https://www.lavozdelsandinismo.com/nicaragua/2020-10-19/compartimos-la-alegria-del-pueblo-boliviano-que-hoy-ha-visto-triunfar-sus-suenos/|url-status=dead}}</ref> The United States Secretary of State, [[Mike Pompeo]], sent congratulations to Arce for his victory and expressed hope that the United States and Bolivia could work together on joint interests in the future.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.infobae.com/america/america-latina/2020/10/19/estados-unidos-felicito-a-luis-arce-por-su-victoria-en-bolivia-esperamos-trabajar-en-nuestros-intereses-conjuntos/|title=The United States congratulated Luis Arce on his victory in Bolivia: "We hope to work in our joint interests."|date=19 October 2020|language=es}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.paginasiete.bo/nacional/2020/10/21/pompeo-felicita-al-binomio-del-mas-eeuu-espera-trabajar-con-el-gobierno-elegido-272337.html|title=Pompeo congratulates the MAS binomial: the US hopes to work with the elected government|date=22 October 2020|language=es}}</ref> Arce has indicated that he is open to working with the US in the future after nine years of broken diplomatic relations as well as resuming diplomatic ties with Venezuela and Cuba, which were broken during the period of the interim government.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.paginasiete.bo/nacional/2020/10/22/relaciones-diplomaticas-luis-arce-eeuu-se-lanzan-guinos-272384.html|title=Diplomatic relations: Luis Arce and the US wink at each other|date=22 October 2020|language=es}}</ref> A statement from the Brazilian foreign ministry congratulated Arce and expressed the nation's "willingness to work with the new Bolivian authorities to seek the implementation of initiatives of common interest in the field of friendship, neighborhood and cooperation ties that unite the two countries and their peoples."<ref>{{cite web|date=24 October 2020|url=https://www.lostiempos.com/actualidad/mundo/20201024/brasil-felicita-arce-propone-estrechar-cooperacion-bilateral|title=Brazil congratulates Arce and proposes closer bilateral cooperation|language=es}}</ref>

Bolivian newspaper ''[[El Deber]]'' called Arce's victory "clear and crushing" and praised him for his conciliatory statements after the result, while also emphasizing that the new president will have to appease MAS's radical wing.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Una clara y aplastante victoria {{!}} EL DEBER|url=https://eldeber.com.bo/edicion-impresa/una-clara-y-aplastante-victoria_205213|access-date=2020-10-27|website=eldeber.com.bo|date=19 October 2020 |language=es}}</ref> Writing on ''[[Los Tiempos]]'', Oscar Díaz Arnau attributed Arce's victory to MAS's strong support in rural areas, the weakness of Mesa's candidacy, Arce's moderation, lack of connection between the opposition and rural inhabitants and the candidacy of [[Luis Fernando Camacho]] splitting anti-MAS voters and weakening the opposition.<ref>{{Cite web|date=2020-10-26|title=Razones para una victoria y para una derrota|url=https://www.lostiempos.com/actualidad/opinion/20201026/columna/razones-victoria-derrota|access-date=2020-10-27|website=Los Tiempos|language=es}}</ref>

==Aftermath==
On 25 October, several right-wing and conservative civic organizations in Santa Cruz like the Pro-Santa Cruz Civic Committee and the [[Santa Cruz Youth Union]], both allies of right-wing candidate Luis Fernando Camacho, claimed that Luis Arce was not the president-elect due to alleged fraud. Camacho and his political allies called for strikes around the country.<ref>[https://correodelsur.com/politica/20201104_camacho-se-suma-al-paro-convocado-por-civicos-de-santa-cruz.html Camacho se suma al paro convocado por cívicos de Santa Cruz]</ref><ref>[https://correodelsur.com/politica/20201104_camacho-se-suma-al-paro-convocado-por-civicos-de-santa-cruz.html El oriente boliviano prepara protestas para la toma de posesión del delfín de Evo Morales]</ref><ref>[https://en.mercopress.com/2020/11/06/conservatives-in-bolivia-protest-against-the-inauguration-of-president-elect-arce Conservatives in Bolivia protest against the inauguration of president elect Arce]</ref><ref>{{Cite web|date=2020-10-25|title=Santa Cruz no acepta la victoria de MAS y denuncia fraude|url=https://www.lavanguardia.com/internacional/20201025/492571151/bolivia-ultraderecha-santa-cruz-se-revela-evo-morales.html|access-date=2020-11-20|website=La Vanguardia|language=es}}</ref> 

In order to mitigate their loss of the two-thirds [[supermajority]] in the legislature, MAS parliamentarians used the last few days of the outgoing assembly to make 21 changes to the rules of procedure that formerly required a two-thirds majority so that they could now be passed with only a simple majority.<ref>{{Cite web|title=MAS elimina los dos tercios del Senado con 11 cambios al reglamento|url=https://www.paginasiete.bo/nacional/2020/10/28/mas-elimina-los-dos-tercios-del-senado-con-11-cambios-al-reglamento-273093.html|access-date=2020-11-20|website=www.paginasiete.bo|language=es}}</ref> Some opposition parliamentarians left the session in protest.<ref>{{cite web|date=28 October 2020|title=MAS eliminates two-thirds of the Senate with 11 changes to the regulations|url=https://www.paginasiete.bo/nacional/2020/10/28/mas-elimina-los-dos-tercios-del-senado-con-11-cambios-al-reglamento-273093.html|language=es}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|date=27 October 2020|title=In the last session, MAS benches approved reforms that will prevent the future opposition from being audited|url=https://www.lostiempos.com/actualidad/pais/20201027/ultima-sesion-bancadas-del-mas-aprueban-reformas-que-impediran|language=es}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|date=27 October 2020|title=MAS in the Senate eliminates two-thirds for 11 decisions, including promotions|url=https://www.opinion.com.bo/articulo/pais/mas-senado-elimina-tercios-11-decisiones-incluyendo-ascensos/20201027221924793144.html|language=es}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|date=27 October 2020|title=Senate and Deputies change regulations to avoid two thirds|url=https://eldeber.com.bo/usted-elige/senado-y-diputados-cambian-reglamentos-para-evitar-los-dos-tercios_206392|language=es}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|date=2020-11-17|title=Antidemocrático – Antidemocratic|url=https://bolivianthoughts.com/2020/11/17/antidemocratico-antidemocratic/|access-date=2020-11-20|website=Bolivian Thoughts in an Emerging World|language=en}}</ref> Opposition leader Carlos Mesa condemned the changes, saying "Authoritarianism, abuse and the submission of the Legislative Assembly continue".<ref>{{cite web|date=27 October 2020|title=The MAS modifies regulations and eliminates two thirds in the Senate in the last session|url=https://www.lostiempos.com/actualidad/pais/20201027/mas-modifica-reglamento-elimina-dos-tercios-senado-ultima-sesion|language=es}}</ref> MAS Senator Omar Aguilar supported the amendments, asking, "Are we going to block the governance of Luis Arce just because we lack three senators in this chamber?"<ref>{{cite web|date=27 October 2020|title=Aguilar: The modification is to give governance to Arce Catacora|url=https://www.paginasiete.bo/nacional/2020/10/27/aguilar-la-modificacion-es-para-darle-gobernabilidad-arce-catacora-273035.html|language=es}}</ref> The corresponding session in the House of Deputies lasted less than 20 minutes without any discussion of the amendments being made.<ref>{{cite web|date=28 October 2020|title=MAS deputies eliminated two thirds in less than 20 minutes|url=https://www.lostiempos.com/actualidad/pais/20201028/diputados-del-mas-eliminaron-dos-tercios-menos-20-minutos|language=es}}</ref> Outgoing MAS president of the Senate [[Eva Copa]] said that the amendments will "speed up the legislative task."<ref name="neutralise">{{cite web|date=28 October 2020|title=MAS neutralizes the opposition for 5 years with the endorsement of Arce|url=https://www.paginasiete.bo/nacional/2020/10/29/mas-neutraliza-la-oposicion-por-anos-con-el-aval-de-arce-273212.html|language=es|access-date=26 November 2020|archive-date=18 May 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210518152358/https://www.paginasiete.bo/nacional/2020/10/29/mas-neutraliza-la-oposicion-por-anos-con-el-aval-de-arce-273212.html|url-status=dead}}</ref>

President-elect Arce endorsed the changes, saying that the decision "wakes up [the government]" for the incoming assembly. "What our Assembly has done is maintain legality. There are many laws that are going to be approved with two-thirds. That is established by the regulations and there should be no concern", he said.<ref name="neutralise" />

On 5 November, president-elect Luis Arce was attacked using dynamite at his campaign house in La Paz.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Vocero del MAS denuncia atentado con dinamita en contra de Luis Arce|url=https://www.paginasiete.bo/nacional/2020/11/5/vocero-del-mas-denuncia-atentado-con-dinamita-en-contra-de-luis-arce-273972.html|access-date=2020-11-20|website=www.paginasiete.bo|language=es}}</ref> On 14 November, Jorge Valda, a Pro-Santa Cruz Committee attorney who claimed fraud in the elections, was arrested and sent to La Paz where he was convicted for legitimation of illicit profits.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Detuvieron en Bolivia a uno de los abogados que denunció fraude y pidió que se auditen las elecciones|url=https://www.infobae.com/america/america-latina/2020/11/14/detuvieron-en-bolivia-a-uno-de-los-abogados-que-denuncio-fraude-y-pidio-que-se-auditen-las-elecciones/|access-date=2020-11-20|website=infobae|date=14 November 2020 |language=es-ES}}</ref> Arce was inaugurated on 8 November 2020.

In June 2021, ''[[The Intercept]]'' obtained audio of officials of the outgoing government and the military plotting a second coup. The plans involved the use of mercenaries from the United States. [[Luis Fernando López (military)|Luis Fernando López]], former defense minister, was recorded saying that Sergio Orellana, the top general, was involved in the plot. Orellana fled the country upon Arce's victory.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://theintercept.com/2021/06/17/bolivia-coup-plot-mercenaries/|title=Bolivian Ex-Minister of Defense Plotted a Second Coup Using U.S. Mercenaries|date=17 June 2021 }}</ref>

=== Legacy ===
On 1 February 2021, the government of Luis Arce declared 18 October 2020, the date of the general elections, to be the "Day of recovery of intercultural democracy".<ref>{{Cite web|title=Gobierno declara al 18 de de octubre Día de la Recuperación de la Democracia|url=https://www.opinion.com.bo/articulo/pais/gobierno-declara-18-octubre-dia-recuperacion-democracia/20210201164254806133.html|access-date=2021-02-01|website=Opinión Bolivia|date=February 2021 |language=es}}</ref> Previously, 10 October 1982 has been considered the day of Bolivia's return to democracy as it was the date in which [[Guido Vildoso]] and the military returned power to the democratically elected [[Hernán Siles Zuazo]]. The decree instructs that the ministries, in coordination with the Autonomous Territorial Entities, as well as social organizations and civil society, organize activities to celebrate democratic values, the reestablishment and preservation of intercultural democratic institutions. The move was criticised by Carlos Mesa who called it "an affront to the citizens who conquered democracy on 10/10/82."<ref>{{Cite web|title=Mesa califica de afrenta que Arce decrete día de la "recuperación de la democracia"|url=https://www.paginasiete.bo/nacional/2021/2/1/mesa-califica-de-afrenta-que-arce-decrete-dia-de-la-recuperacion-de-la-democracia-283049.html|access-date=2021-02-01|website=www.paginasiete.bo|language=spanish}}</ref>

